{"id":3544,"date":"2026-03-29T10:23:21","date_gmt":"2026-03-29T10:23:21","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/cde-me.com\/?p=3544"},"modified":"2026-03-29T20:06:10","modified_gmt":"2026-03-29T20:06:10","slug":"thermographic-inspection","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/cde-me.com\/thermographic-inspection\/","title":{"rendered":"Thermographic Inspection"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Introduction<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Many defects within a structure are not visible through conventional inspection methods. Moisture intrusion, insulation failure, and energy loss often remain hidden until they cause significant damage.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Thermographic inspection provides a non-destructive way to detect such hidden issues.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is Thermographic Inspection<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Thermographic inspection uses infrared imaging to detect temperature variations within a structure. These variations indicate underlying issues such as moisture, voids, or insulation defects.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Our Approach<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. Infrared Survey<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The structure is scanned using thermal imaging equipment to detect temperature differences.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Data Interpretation<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Thermal images are analyzed to identify anomalies and potential defects.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. Defect Identification<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Areas affected by moisture intrusion, insulation failure, or energy loss are identified.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. Reporting<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Findings are documented with images and technical explanations.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Scope of Services<\/h2>